<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<inkscape-extension xmlns="http://www.inkscape.org/namespace/inkscape/extension">
    <name>Dimension Line</name>
    <id>org.markus.architecture.dimension_line</id>

    <param name="tab" type="notebook">
        <page name="opts" gui-text="Options">
            <param name="from" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="When TWO objects are selected, take points from:">
                <option value="ends">Path endpoints (start node of each)</option>
                <option value="centers">Bounding-box centers</option>
            </param>
            <label appearance="header">Tip: select a SINGLE line/path to dimension from its start node to its end node. The option above only applies when two objects are selected.</label>
            <param name="unit" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="Display unit:">
                <option value="mm">mm</option>
                <option value="cm">cm</option>
                <option value="m">m</option>
                <option value="px">px</option>
            </param>
            <param name="precision" type="int" min="0" max="6"
                   gui-text="Decimal places:">0</param>
            <param name="suffix" type="bool"
                   gui-text="Append unit after the value">false</param>
            <param name="offset" type="float" min="-1000.0" max="1000.0"
                   precision="2" gui-text="Line offset (mm, 0 = on the points):">5.0</param>
            <param name="ext" type="float" min="0.0" max="200.0"
                   precision="2" gui-text="Witness extension (mm):">1.5</param>
            <param name="ends" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="End marks:">
                <option value="arrow">Arrow (filled triangle)</option>
                <option value="openarrow">Open arrow (stroked)</option>
                <option value="tick">Tick / slash (45°, architect)</option>
                <option value="dot">Dot (filled circle)</option>
                <option value="none">None</option>
            </param>
            <param name="arrow" type="float" min="0.0" max="50.0"
                   precision="2" gui-text="End mark size (mm, 0 = none):">2.5</param>
            <param name="stroke_width" type="float" min="0.01" max="20.0"
                   precision="2" gui-text="Stroke width (mm):">0.25</param>
            <param name="stroke_color" type="color" gui-text="Stroke color:">255</param>
            <separator/>
            <param name="notext" type="bool"
                   gui-text="No text (draw geometry only)">false</param>
            <param name="textpos" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="Text position:">
                <option value="above">Above the line</option>
                <option value="below">Below the line</option>
                <option value="center">Centered on the line (covers it)</option>
            </param>
            <param name="fontsize" type="float" min="1.0" max="100.0"
                   precision="2" gui-text="Font size (px):">10.0</param>
            <param name="fontfamily" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="Font:">
                <option value="sans-serif">sans-serif (default)</option>
                <option value="serif">serif</option>
                <option value="monospace">monospace</option>
                <option value="Arial">Arial</option>
                <option value="Helvetica">Helvetica</option>
                <option value="IBM Plex Sans">IBM Plex Sans</option>
                <option value="Open Sans">Open Sans</option>
                <option value="Univers">Univers</option>
                <option value="Aptos">Aptos</option>
                <option value="Calibri">Calibri</option>
                <option value="Times New Roman">Times New Roman</option>
                <option value="Verdana">Verdana</option>
            </param>
            <param name="fontcustom" type="string"
                   gui-text="Custom font (overrides the list if not empty):"></param>
            <separator/>
            <param name="hide_source" type="bool"
                   gui-text="Make the source line invisible after dimensioning (stroke:none, stays selectable; single-line mode)">true</param>
        </page>
        <page name="update" gui-text="Update">
            <param name="on_existing" type="optiongroup" appearance="combo"
                   gui-text="When an existing dimension is selected:">
                <option value="refresh">Refresh from source (keep its stored style)</option>
                <option value="restyle">Re-apply the settings on the Options tab</option>
            </param>
            <label xml:space="preserve">Each dimension is one group tagged with the
id of its source object and all its settings.

Select a dimension (or its hidden source line)
and run the extension again to rebuild it from
the source's CURRENT position — so after you
move or edit the line, one run updates the
dimension. Assign a keyboard shortcut under
Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Interface &gt; Keyboard,
search "Dimension Line", for one-key updates.

"Refresh" keeps the look stored in the group.
"Re-apply" restyles it with the Options tab
values (the dialog can't pre-load the stored
ones, so use this when you want to change style).

The source line is made invisible (stroke:none),
not removed, so it stays selectable on the canvas
(click / Tab / rubber-band) and its nodes stay
editable. Move or edit it, then re-run to update.</label>
        </page>
        <page name="var" gui-text="Variable">
            <param name="usevar" type="bool"
                   gui-text="Replace value with a variable">false</param>
            <param name="varname" type="string"
                   gui-text="Variable text:">{B}</param>
            <param name="var_italic" type="bool"
                   gui-text="Italic symbol (upright index)">true</param>
            <label xml:space="preserve">When enabled, the measured number is replaced
by the text above (e.g. {B}, L1, b_eff). The
geometry is still placed using the real distance,
so you can toggle this without moving anything.

Subscripts / superscripts:
  t_CLT        -> t with CLT as subscript
  f_{m,CLT}    -> braces group multi-part indices
  A^2          -> superscript
The index is always UPRIGHT; with "Italic symbol"
the base letter is italic (ISO quantity style:
italic symbol, upright index), as in t_CLT.
Braces without _ or ^ stay literal, so {B} is
unchanged.

The label is SVG text, so a later find/replace
across the file updates every instance at once.</label>
        </page>
        <page name="help" gui-text="Help">
            <label xml:space="preserve">Two ways to use it:

ONE line/path selected (easiest):
Just draw a line between the two points you want
to measure and run. The dimension goes from the
path's first node to its last node. The path may
be a combined path or live inside a group.

TWO objects selected:
"Path endpoints" uses the first node of each
selected path. "Bounding-box centers" uses each
object's center (handy for two dots/crosses).

A dimension line with witness lines, arrowheads
and a distance label is added to the layer of the
first selection. Offset places the line parallel,
clear of the geometry; set offset = 0 to draw it
directly between the two points.</label>
        </page>
    </param>

    <effect>
        <object-type>all</object-type>
        <effects-menu>
            <submenu name="Architecture"/>
        </effects-menu>
    </effect>

    <script>
        <command location="inx" interpreter="python">dimension_line.py</command>
    </script>
</inkscape-extension>
